        "text": "Technically, cryptocurrencies are a single asset class. But in a cryptocurrency portfolio, you can diversify across products, coins, and tokens that present different goals and use cases. For example, one way to allocate a portfolio could be 40% bitcoins, 30% stablecoins, 15% NFTs, and 15% altcoins. Most advice will tell you that your crypto portfolio has to be diversified. While it is a standard practice for investors, there are pros and cons to spreading your capital around different assets. A diversified portfolio reduces overall risk and volatility. Losses can be offset by gains. To keep your position stable, your portfolio also has more opportunities to make gains with each additional coin you own. However, the more diversified your portfolio is, the closer it will track the overall market. Most traders and investors are looking to beat the market with larger gains. A highly diversified portfolio will lead to more average returns than a successfully concentrated portfolio.",
